WEBVTT

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.980
Schick, first in electric shaving, now brings you Dragnet.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:21.870
Ladies and gentlemen, the story you are about to see is true.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.720
The names have been changed to protect the innocent.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:57.480
City, Angeles, California. I work here. It's Thursday, November 19th. Clear in Los Angeles.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.500
We were working the day watch out of Homicide Division.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.180
My partner's Frank Smith. The boss is Captain Lorman.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.620
My name's Friday.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.730
Earlier that morning, we'd received a call from Georgia Street.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.360
A girl had just been brought in.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.770
She was in critical condition.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.820
Apparently, she tried to kill herself.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.400
...how smooth your face can feel

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.960
when you shave with a Schick 25 electric shaver.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.970
No matter how tough your beard, no matter how...

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:36.630
tender your skin. The Schick 25 can give you a close, comfortable shave on all parts of

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:42.660
your face. And when you're finished, your face feels almost as smooth as the face of

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:49.920
a little boy. Boy, oh boy, really smooth. And your Schick will give you that closer shave

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:57.170
with fewer strokes. Why? Because Schick and Only Schick has these comb-edged shaving heads

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.600
that actually comb your whiskers up straight.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:07.100
closer shaving. And along with his closer shave, you get Schick's exclusive colors for men. Remember,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.820
your dealer will give you a $7.50 trade-in allowance on any old electric shaver, any standard

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:27.370
make. Enjoy closer shave. Get a new Schick 25 tomorrow. How's she doing, Doc? Pretty hard to say

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.510
yet. We just finished with a transfusion. Uh-huh.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.830
She's got a chance of pulling through, but there's no way of telling how much damage has been done to the brain tissue.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:34.430
I see.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.830
What about the bruise on her face?

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:36.950
Might have happened when she fell.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.990
I never knew you gave transfusions in a case like this, Doc.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:41.830
We don't, unless the patient's critical.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:47.700
What happens is the carbon monoxide in the gas joins with the hemoglobin in the red cells, won't let go.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.930
Then the blood takes the monoxide through the system and suffocates the brain tissue.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.940
We're also giving her coramine to speed up the heart action.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:55.900
It's a rough one, all right.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.440
Did you find out who she is yet?

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.980
Well, according to the stuff in her wallet, her name's Mona Fenton.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.380
According to the hotel where they found her,

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.160
she was registered as Mrs. John Loras.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.370
Maybe she just got married.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:06.600
That's possible.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.060
Identification card in her wallet

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.420
shows her mother is next of kin.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.120
Here's an address and a phone number.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.480
We called, but nobody answers.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.280
Well, if you reach anybody who knows her,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.160
ask them something for me.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.050
Sure, what's that?

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.340
Find out if the girl's been under a doctor's care.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:18.890
Huh?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.720
I checked her over when she came in, found some marks.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:22.620
On her arms?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:23.370
Yes.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.690
I think she's an addict.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.960
At approximately 8.30 a.m. that morning,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.300
the desk clerk in a small hotel on Grand Street had detected the odor of gas in

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:38.020
one of the halls of the building. Using a passkey he had entered the room which

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:44.630
was presumably occupied by Mr. and Mrs. John Loras. He found a girl sprawled

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:48.230
across the bed unconscious. The gas heater had been turned on full and the

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.830
windows had been locked and stuffed with pieces of torn sheets. The clerk had

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.340
immediately aired out the room and called an ambulance. The girl was removed

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.970
to Georgia Street Hospital and was still in an unconscious state. Dr. Hall said he

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.900
get in touch with us as soon as her condition improved we left the hospital

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.980
and drove out to the hotel

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:46.310
Has anybody else been in here since the other officers left?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:46.950
No, sir.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.490
They told me to lock it up until the fellas from Homicide got here.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.660
That's you guys, isn't it?

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:51.120
That's right.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.320
Everything is just the way you found it, is that right?

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.110
Well, yeah.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.950
Of course, the gas is turned off and opened the windows,

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.270
but everything else is the same.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.740
Over the phone, you said she moved in last night.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.360
Yes, sir. At least that's what the registration book says.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.720
They checked in at 10.15, her and her husband.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.470
You weren't on duty at the time, were you?

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:07.730
No, I was out to dinner.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:08.630
Who checked them in?

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.010
Jeff. Jeff Christensen.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:10.940
Is he around?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.540
No, not right now, but he'll probably be back tonight.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.780
You know where we can find him now?

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.080
Afraid not. You see, Jeff's sort of our handyman.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.160
He takes care of the building.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.860
Once in a while, when I got something to do, he handles the desk.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.900
This his day off?

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.800
It's not supposed to be, but you see, he got paid last night.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.400
That means he's probably celebrating.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:28.960
Jeff starts celebrating, he's kind of hard to track down.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:29.960
Do you have his home address?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.960
He lives here.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.040
A hotel gives him a room.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:32.720
I see.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.560
Will he be back tonight?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:34.440
Yeah.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.200
He only worked a couple of days last week,

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:38.040
so he ain't gonna be able to really tie one on.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:38.920
Uh-huh.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.860
You get a look at the man who came in with the girl?

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.770
No, they were already in the room when I got back from dinner.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.570
I checked the book and got the money from Jeff before he shoved off.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.200
Man must have left sometime earlier this morning.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.420
Guess I was asleep.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.140
My room's just back at the desk.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.940
He must have got out while I was catnapping.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.060
Now, how about calls?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:55.720
Did they make any?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:56.990
Nope, not a one.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.880
Like I told those uniformed officers that were here before.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.420
I didn't hear a peep out of them.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.240
Matter of fact, I was thinking how nice and quiet they were.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.500
But the way the room looks, they sure

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.820
must have had some sort of argument.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:09.270
Yes, sir.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.650
Do you know if they brought any baggage in with them?

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.240
Matter of fact, no, they didn't.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.540
That's the reason Jeff got the money for the room in advance.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:16.520
Always do.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.420
If they ain't got luggage, they got to pay in advance.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.510
Sure looks like they did some heavy drinking, don't it?

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:22.180
Uh-huh.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.460
That bottle's almost empty.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.480
I'd rather you wouldn't touch anything.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:25.220
Oh, sure.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.380
I'll call the lab.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:26.680
Right.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.500
Say, have you talked to the girl's family?

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:29.420
No, sir, not yet.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:29.960
You're planning to...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.780
to see them, aren't you?

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:31.500
Yes, we are.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.880
Wonder if you'd do me a favor.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:33.790
What's that?

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.810
Well, I don't much mind the dirty glasses

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:36.910
and having to clean the room up.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.170
That's part of the hotel business.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.810
But I wish you'd say something about the way

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.850
she ripped up these sheets.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.220
Maybe if her folks know about it, they'll pay for them.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.620
You will mention it, won't you?

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:45.810
Yes, sir.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.730
Now, who else has a passkey to this room?

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:48.770
You mean besides me?

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:49.310
That's right.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.100
Nobody.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.380
Well, what do you usually keep it?

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.590
Hangs on a nail next to the desk.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.110
When you first came in here this morning,

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.050
was there anything around the door to keep the gas

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:57.570
from escaping?

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:58.820
Let me think.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:00.550
I remember.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.620
No, there wasn't nothing at the door,

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.360
just those torn sheets around the windows.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.140
Was the key in the lock?

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:07.470
You mean inside the room?

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.220
That's right.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.720
No, the reason I'm sure is I looked through the keyhole,

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.240
tried to see what was going on.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.050
If the key had been there, I'd have noticed it.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:14.550
Uh-huh.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:15.900
Lab crews on the way.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:16.360
Good.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:17.640
I talked to Doc Hall.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:18.470
How's the girl?

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:19.710
About the same, still critical.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.190
Said they were going to move her to general.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.210
Oh, sure hope she doesn't die.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.070
That's all we need.

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:24.610
What's that?

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.930
Being in the papers gives the place a bad name.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.540
It's hard enough to run a hotel without having someone

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:29.920
and use it.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.300
knock themselves off now you guys will be all over the place other tenants ain't gonna like it

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.120
why'd it have to happen here that's what I'd like to know well there's something we'd like to know

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:52.420
yeah why'd it have to happen anyplace talk to the occupants in adjacent rooms none of them

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:59.750
remembered hearing a quarrel or any other unusual noises during the previous night the crime lab

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.410
the room thoroughly under the bed they found an empty capsule it looked like it might have

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:09.690
contained heroin two clear sets of prints were obtained from the drinking glasses the prints

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:16.640
were photographed and the glasses were booked as evidence the hotel registration card was given to

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:25.910
larry sloan in handwriting the names john loris mona loris and mona fenton were checked through

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.980
R&I. There was nothing on any of them.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.960
We asked the hotel clerk to contact us as soon as the handyman returned.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.840
We also asked him to let us know in the event the man who called himself John Loras came back.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:45.670
We checked Mona Fenton's home on Highland Avenue, 12.16 p.m.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.710
We talked to her mother.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.620
You're sure it's Mona?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.320
According to the identification in her pocketbook, yes.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.400
It just doesn't seem possible.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.450
I guess I should have expected it, though.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:56.440
Ma'am?

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.860
I warned her. I told her it would never work out.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.560
Children are all alike. They won't listen.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.420
You try to talk to them and they say things have changed.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.220
You're too old to keep up with the times.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.530
Well, she's got nobody but herself to blame now.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:10.640
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.940
A girl like her leaving school and taking a job in a restaurant.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.740
Most ridiculous thing I ever heard of.

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:19.350
If she was still in college, none of this would have happened.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.930
Can you think of any reason why your daughter might want to take her own life?

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.430
I'd be the last one to know.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.020
Mona hasn't confided in me for some time.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:29.170
I see.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:35.350
We had quite an argument I haven't talked to her for over a month. Well doesn't she live here miss Fenton?

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:41.120
She has her own room with an outside entrance. She comes and goes as she pleases, but I hardly ever see her

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:46.560
I didn't even know she wasn't here last night unless you've been ill recently not to my knowledge

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:51.200
Why oh we wonder if your daughter had been under a doctor's care. Oh, I don't think so

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:59.520
She's always been a healthy girl. Are you acquainted with Mona's friends miss Fenton? I used to meet them occasionally not

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.000
was she engaged would you know I don't think so there was one boy she went with

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.940
more than any of the others what's his name Richard Burdick seemed to be a nice

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.140
young fellow he and Mona talked about being married but they were going to

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:18.500
wait until they finished school of course when she left college they broke

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:24.950
up they have a fight well I wouldn't call it that they agreed to disagree you

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:28.410
might say was Mona's idea Richard was still in love with her

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:41.040
Does your daughter have any other close friends, Fenton?

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:49.540
I suppose I might as well tell you, Mona isn't actually my daughter.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:50.380
Oh.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:53.530
You see, I was your father's second wife.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.890
Her own mother died when Mona was just a child.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.870
I tried to take her place, but I think Mona always resented.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.690
I don't blame her for that yes, ma'am and when her father died. I was all she had

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:16.130
She was all I had to maybe I overdid it trying to be both mother and father for a child that wasn't mine

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:21.560
It was a little girl. We used to be so much alike. Nobody would have guessed. She wasn't my own

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:29.670
We even wore the same dresses all of a sudden she withdrew wasn't part of her life anymore

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:35.480
I don't suppose she's asked to see me, even now.

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:36.700
Well, she's still unconscious.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.100
You're being kind, aren't you, Sergeant?

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:40.430
No, ma'am, that's the truth.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.630
I won't go to her unless she wants me.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:43.790
I have some pride, too.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:44.660
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.390
Now, this boy your daughter used to go with,

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:47.540
what's his name, Richard Burdick?

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:48.370
That's right.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:49.720
One day breakup.

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:51.660
Oh, seven or eight weeks ago.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.410
Was Mona despondent after that?

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:56.500
A few times I saw her, she seemed to be in good spirits.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.360
Do you know what caused the breakup?

00:11:59.330 --> 00:11:59.910
Not really.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.360
She said her new job was more important than Richard.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.100
She kept breaking dates, standing him up.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.380
Did Mona have any other steady boyfriends?

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:08.870
There was one young man.

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:11.210
Matter of fact, he's quite a little bit older than she is.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.030
He's picked her up several times in the last month.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:15.190
Do you know his name?

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:16.770
No, I never met him.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:20.010
I saw his car parked out in front several times.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:21.940
He'd drive up and honk the horn.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.580
He never came inside.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.300
What kind of a car does he drive, do you know?

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.650
I don't think it's an American car.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:28.430
English, maybe.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:29.980
Some kind of a...

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.640
I see. Do you know the color?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.430
He's only been here in the evenings when it was dark.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:36.230
I couldn't say.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.210
Did she ever mention this man by name?

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:41.150
No. She carefully avoided mentioning his name.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.490
How often have they been out together?

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.500
Four or five times that I know of.

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:46.920
Of course, they may have had other dates.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.150
Would you recognize him?

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:50.500
I'm afraid not.

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:52.260
But you did say he was older than Mona.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:52.840
That's right.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:54.730
Well, how did you know that?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.140
The first time I saw her meet him, when she came home,

00:12:58.180 --> 00:12:59.980
I asked her what sort of a person he was.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:01.750
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.720
She said there was one thing in his favor,

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.080
that he wasn't an immature child like Richard Burdick,

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:08.800
that he was an adult.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:10.400
Oh, I see.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:12.560
What about Mona's other friends?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.750
Well, they're the girls she works with.

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:18.860
I don't know their names, except one of them.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:19.670
Who's that?

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:21.500
Peggy, Peggy Gregson.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.080
During one of our arguments,

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.660
Mona threatened to move out of the house

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.060
and take an apartment with Peggy.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:28.860
I don't know whether she was serious or not.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.120
Where is this restaurant where your daughter works?

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:35.110
It's on Olympic Boulevard near Robertson.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.050
Would you know the name of it?

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:40.930
Blue Peacock Cafe, I think it's called.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.390
Do you know the names of any of her other friends?

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.820
No. During the last two or three months,

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:48.840
she has deliberately avoided seeing any of the people she used to know.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.980
Did she ever have a boyfriend named John?

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:55.130
I think there was a boy in high school she had a couple of dates with.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.210
What was his last name? Do you remember?

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.290
Brewster, I believe, yes.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.410
That's right, John Brewster.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:05.250
Does the name John Loris sound familiar to you?

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:06.200
Loris?

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.900
Yes, ma'am. L-O-R-R-I-S.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.400
No. No, I've never heard Mona speak of him.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.240
All right, Ms. Fenton. Thank you very much.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.340
Well, they let me know how she's getting along.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.820
Well, they're moving her to the general hospital. You can call them there.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:23.300
Before you go.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:24.250
Ma'am.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.810
All these questions about Mona's friends and acquaintances.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:31.830
Can't help being puzzled.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:32.680
What about?

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.630
Do you police always go into such detail?

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:40.950
I mean, you said it was an attempted suicide, didn't you?

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:42.080
Well, it looks that way.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.260
We aren't sure yet, Miss Fennin.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:44.930
What else could it have been?

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:46.960
Well, we're just checking it out now.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.200
You mean somebody might have tried to kill Mona?

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:54.410
No, ma'am, we didn't say that.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:58.240
You're very discreet, aren't you, Sergeant?

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:10.220
Hello, yes, it's what?

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:12.950
Yes, they're here.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:13.790
Just a moment.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:15.580
Thank you.

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:16.730
This Friday.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:21.320
Doc, I have to say.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.800
Yeah, right.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.350
By the way, we have to be leaving Miss Fenton.

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.550
That call, was it about Mona?

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:29.490
Yes, ma'am, it was.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:29.970
Something...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:36.480
happened well has it i've got a right to know she's worse isn't she yes ma'am she's had a relapse

