And your dealer has them all right now.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:03.350
We drove over to the Blue Peacock Cafe on Olympic Boulevard.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.120
You wanted to see me?

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.240
Are you Peggy Gregson?

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.000
Yeah, why?

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.000
We're police officers.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:15.900
Would you like to talk to you for a minute?

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:16.740
What about?

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:17.740
Just a couple questions.

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:19.450
Well, I've got to get the manager's okay.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.250
I'm on duty now.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.650
Sorry, we've already spoken to him.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:22.220
Oh?

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:23.610
Well, hurry it up, will you?

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:24.570
I don't want to miss out on my tips.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.150
I have two tables almost ready to leave.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:26.710
We understand.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:27.980
Like to sit down?

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:29.880
Gee, I don't know.

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:38.390
Okay. What's this all about?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.480
You know a girl named Mona Fenton?

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:41.900
Sure. She works here.

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:43.410
Is she a pretty good friend of yours?

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:44.960
I guess so.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:46.730
Something happened to Mona?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.170
That's right. She didn't show up this morning.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:50.990
She been in an accident?

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:52.740
Not exactly.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:54.720
Well, what is it?

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.540
Ms. Fenton's in the general hospital.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:57.290
Yeah?

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.460
Far as we know, she attempted suicide.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:00.300
Mona?

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.040
That's right.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.300
Why'd she do a thing like that?

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.660
Well, we thought maybe you could help us find out.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.230
I didn't have anything to do with it.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.880
You can't think of any reason she might

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:10.820
try to take her own life.

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:13.740
Not a reason in the world, not Mona.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:15.880
You sure it was suicide?

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:16.720
Why'd he ask?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.970
I was just thinking.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:22.040
Sometimes people try to make it look like a suicide,

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:22.520
don't they?

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.460
Well, what do you mean, Peggy?

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.930
You know, when they kill somebody.

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.390
I'll just bet that's what's happened to Mona.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:28.290
Why'd he say that?

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:29.980
Oh, it's just a .

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.580
Just a hunch.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.250
Did she have any enemies?

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.570
Anybody who might want to kill her?

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:36.430
I wouldn't want to say.

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:38.450
Well, why not?

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:39.290
Mona was your friend.

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:42.150
Just wouldn't want to get somebody else in trouble.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.160
She's in plenty of it already.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.110
He won't find out, will he, if I talk to you?

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:49.490
Who?

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:50.770
Dick Burdick.

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.900
If anybody tried to hurt Mona, it was him.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:53.900
Why do you say that?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:55.720
Because it's true.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.680
I don't think he's all there.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:58.440
Huh?

00:18:58.770 --> 00:18:59.930
You know, in the head.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.160
He's been coming around here for the last month threatening her.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.420
Are you sure he threatened her?

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:06.570
Yeah, I heard him half a dozen times.

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.450
Mona kept telling him to get out.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.940
She didn't want any part of him, to leave her alone.

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.260
He just kept coming back, making more of a nuisance of himself.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.360
When a girl's through with the guy,

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.580
I don't know why he won't shove off.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.020
Was Mona through with Burdick?

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:19.980
Sure.

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.510
She had somebody else on the string.

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:22.550
Who was that, do you know?

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:23.550
Terry.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:24.840
What's his last name?

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.860
Gee, I don't know, but he's a real smooth operator.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.080
I like Burdick.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.100
Drives a jag.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:32.390
There's plenty of dough.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.940
Can't blame Mona for giving Dick the gate when there's a guy like Terry around.

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:37.430
Where does this Terry live, do you know?

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:39.680
Uh-uh. Mona never said.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.930
I guess she was saving him for herself.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:43.450
What's he do for a living?

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:44.800
I don't know.

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.010
Whatever it is, he must be pretty good at it.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.280
The way he throws his money around.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.210
Did Mona ever mention a man named John Loras?

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.440
The name doesn't sound familiar.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.720
When was the last time you saw Mona?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:57.440
Yesterday.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:19:59.710
No, it was the day before yesterday.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:07.440
Was her day off she seemed to be in good spirits best had a date with Terry that night did he pick her up here?

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:14.640
Yeah, about nine o'clock parked outside gave a honk. She was just starting to leave when Bertie came in what happened?

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:22.180
He made another scene told her she had to stop seeing Terry. Yeah told her if he ever saw him together again, he'd kill her

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:37.550
We talked to the other waitresses in the restaurant and they confirmed what Peggy Gregson had told us.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:43.050
We telephoned Mrs. Fenton and got Richard Burdick's address.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:44.580
Thank you.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.360
He lived in a rooming house on Los Feliz Boulevard.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:51.120
The landlady kept telling us what a good tenant he was.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:52.590
She thought he was in his room.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:14.560
Place is clean.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:15.300
Yep.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:16.540
He moved out.

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:17.930
Thank you.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:24.400
Burdick's landlady insisted that she had no idea when or why he had moved out.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:28.680
His rent was paid up to the end of the month, and he had given her no indication that he was leaving.

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:36.290
She gave us Burdick's description and the name and telephone number of his employers.

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:40.390
We put in a call, and they told us that he had failed to report for work that morning.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.970
As far as they knew, he had not quit his job.

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:58.440
Went back to the office and checked his name and description through R&I.

00:21:58.930 --> 00:21:59.970
Apparently, he had no criminal...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.180
criminal record in Los Angeles.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.150
We'll be right back.

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:03.720
Thank you.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.190
We got out a local and an APB.

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:08.520
Thank you.

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:10.900
4 39 p.m.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.960
We got a call from the general hospital stating that the Fenton girl had regained consciousness.

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:17.140
Frank and I drove over code three.

00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:19.130
Thank you.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:55.770
We'd like to talk to you.

00:22:56.300 --> 00:22:57.260
Sick, can't you see that?

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:58.480
I don't want to talk to anybody.

00:22:58.800 --> 00:22:59.900
The doctor said it'd be all right.

00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:01.750
He doesn't know how sick I am.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:02.410
Maybe he does.

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:04.650
Wish they hadn't found me, that's all.

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:06.870
I'd be better off, and so would everybody else.

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:08.670
You tried to kill yourself, is that right?

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:10.320
What did you think I was doing?

00:23:11.190 --> 00:23:12.110
Who were you with last night?

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:12.900
Nobody.

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:14.090
Come on, Miss Fenton.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:15.540
He wasn't with me.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:18.050
He took the room together, but he walked out.

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:19.380
Left me flat.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:20.320
What's his name?

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:20.990
Terry.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:22.200
Terry Hamilton.

00:23:22.970 --> 00:23:25.130
We were going to get married yesterday. That's what he promised.

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:27.210
And it was too late to buy a license.

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:29.280
That was his reason this time.

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:29.970
and I

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.800
I knew it last night.

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:33.770
I knew it was just an excuse, so we had a fight.

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:35.220
I told him to get out.

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:36.520
He hit me.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:37.060
Go on.

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:38.460
That's all that happened.

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:41.380
He slugged me and left, so I decided,

00:23:42.070 --> 00:23:44.530
you know what I decided.

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:48.140
Is that the whole story, Miss Fenton?

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:48.600
Sure.

00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:50.950
Guess I'm not the first girl who got jilted

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:51.890
and tried to kill herself.

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.170
You're leaving something out, aren't you?

00:23:54.630 --> 00:23:55.090
Like what?

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:55.940
You're a user.

00:23:56.670 --> 00:23:57.510
I don't know what you mean.

00:23:57.960 --> 00:23:58.640
I think you do.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.820
When did you start taking him?

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:02.720
When I met Terry.

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:04.500
That was his idea, too.

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.160
I guess that's really all he wanted, just to get me hooked.

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:09.240
First, it wasn't so bad.

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:10.200
I thought I loved him.

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:13.060
Then when I had to have a fix, and that's the only thing

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:16.050
I could think about, he told me I'd have to pay for it.

00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:18.320
It was just a business proposition,

00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:19.460
as far as he was concerned.

00:24:21.200 --> 00:24:23.380
If I got a little money, he'd really turn on the romance.

00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:25.730
When I was broke, he turned off the H.

00:24:26.550 --> 00:24:27.470
I lied to him yesterday.

00:24:27.670 --> 00:24:28.430
He said I had dough.

00:24:29.350 --> 00:24:29.970
I thought I could get him to get him.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.560
to marry me before he found out different.

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:33.920
He found out, though.

00:24:34.760 --> 00:24:36.480
All right, Miss Fenton, just a couple more questions.

00:24:36.840 --> 00:24:37.200
Okay.

00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:38.460
What are they?

00:24:39.140 --> 00:24:40.180
You know Hamilton's address.

00:24:40.940 --> 00:24:41.240
Sure.

00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:44.200
When you get out of the hospital, would you be willing to contact him?

00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:44.940
Make a bye.

00:24:45.770 --> 00:24:46.890
You just tell me when.

00:24:48.460 --> 00:24:48.760
All right.

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:49.980
You better get some rash now.

00:24:50.950 --> 00:24:53.090
Yeah, I guess so. I'm still pretty tired.

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:54.380
Say.

00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:56.060
Do me a favor, would you?

00:24:56.200 --> 00:24:56.560
What's that?

00:24:56.980 --> 00:24:59.460
There's a boy I used to go with. His name's Richard Burdick.

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:01.140
Would you get in touch with him?

00:25:01.400 --> 00:25:03.160
Tell him what happened, ask him to come and see me.

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:04.920
We've been trying to find Burdick.

00:25:05.240 --> 00:25:06.160
Looks like he left town.

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:07.360
Mm-hmm.

00:25:08.150 --> 00:25:09.210
That's my fault, too.

00:25:09.740 --> 00:25:10.180
What do you mean?

00:25:10.550 --> 00:25:13.130
I telephoned him yesterday and told him I was going to get married.

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:15.960
He was upset and tried to talk me out of it.

00:25:16.280 --> 00:25:16.980
I wouldn't listen.

00:25:17.850 --> 00:25:19.850
He said I was the only reason he stayed in Los Angeles.

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:22.730
Maybe we'll hear from him.

00:25:23.670 --> 00:25:25.070
I was wrong about everything, wasn't I?

00:25:26.170 --> 00:25:27.390
What I tried to do last night.

00:25:27.610 --> 00:25:27.930
dick.

00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:29.040
My mom everything.

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:30.940
Kind of looks like you were.

00:25:31.590 --> 00:25:32.210
Funny, isn't it?

00:25:33.060 --> 00:25:34.600
I've always thought of her as my stepmother.

00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:35.160
Oh.

00:25:35.850 --> 00:25:37.310
That's the first time I've ever called her mom.

